@page "/Automation"
@model Praja.Web.Pages.Automation.IndexModel
@{ViewData["Title"]="Automatic intake";}
<div class="page-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">AUTOMATIC INTAKE</span><h1>Complaints prepared for review.</h1><p class="muted">Collect, detect, extract and draft automatically. Review once before registration.</p></div><span class="badge @(Model.State.Enabled?"closed":"draft")">@(Model.State.Enabled?"Running":"Paused")</span></div>
@if(Model.Notice is not null){<p class="notice" role="status">@Model.Notice</p>}
<section class="panel form-panel"><h2>Gmail Inbox automation</h2><p><strong>Mailbox:</strong> @Model.Mailbox · @(Model.Connected?"Connected":"Connect Gmail first")</p><p>Inspects Inbox emails without applying a Gmail label. Local rules select likely complaints. Messages not detected as complaints appear below for an officer to check in Gmail. Likely complaints are retained and sent to the configured AI service for extraction and drafting. Review uncertain matches; this detector can miss complaints. No emails are sent or changed.</p><p class="field-help">Checks every 60 seconds while this app is running. Each run considers up to 100 Inbox IDs, reads up to 20 unseen supported text emails and prepares up to 5 pending drafts. HTML bodies are converted to text. Up to three attachments are supported: UTF-8 .txt (64 KiB each) and PDFs (8 MiB total, up to 10 pages each). Text PDFs stay local. Scanned or mixed PDFs are sent in full to the configured AI service before complaint detection, including PDFs that may turn out to be unrelated. Review OCR text against the original. Combined text must fit 6,000 characters. Unsupported files exclude the whole email; review those in Gmail. Attachment binaries are not retained.</p>
@if(!Model.State.Enabled){<form method="post" asp-page-handler="Enable"><label class="check-row consent"><input asp-for="Permission" required/><span>I authorise automatic read-only Inbox collection, local retention of likely complaints and processing of those complaints and scanned PDF attachments by the configured AI service.</span></label><button class="button primary">Enable automatic intake</button></form>}else{<div class="form-actions"><form method="post" asp-page-handler="Run" data-busy><button class="button primary">Run now</button></form><form method="post" asp-page-handler="Pause"><button class="button secondary">Pause automation</button></form></div>}
<p><a class="text-link" href="/GmailSettings">Gmail connection settings</a></p><p><strong>Last run:</strong> @(Model.State.LastRunUtc?.ToString("dd MMM yyyy HH:mm 'UTC'")??"Not run")</p><p role="status">@Model.State.Status</p></section>
@if(Model.State.ManualReview.Any(r=>r.Mailbox==Model.Mailbox)){
<section class="panel form-panel"><h2>Emails needing manual review</h2><p>Latest 50 references retained across mailboxes. These emails were unsupported, oversized or moved out of the Inbox. No partial complaint was imported. Review in Gmail and capture a reviewed transcript in Intake inbox, or use labelled Gmail preview. Previously skipped messages are not automatically retried.</p>
<form method="post" asp-page-handler="RetrySkipped"><button class="button secondary" type="submit">Retry skipped emails</button></form><p class="field-help">Rechecks listed emails in this mailbox on the next run. Scanned PDFs use the configured AI service.</p>
<ul>
@foreach(var mail in Model.State.ManualReview.Where(r=>r.Mailbox==Model.Mailbox)){
<li><a href="@("https://mail.google.com/mail/?authuser="+Uri.EscapeDataString(mail.Mailbox)+"#all/"+Uri.EscapeDataString(mail.MessageId))" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Review Gmail message @mail.MessageId</a></li>
}</ul></section>}
@if(Model.State.NonComplaintReview.Any(r=>r.Mailbox==Model.Mailbox)){
<section class="panel form-panel"><h2>Emails not detected as complaints</h2>
<p>Local rules can miss indirect wording. Check these messages in Gmail. Only the latest 50 message references are saved across mailboxes; bodies and subjects are not retained here. Older messages classified before this feature are not listed.</p>
@foreach(var mail in Model.State.NonComplaintReview.Where(r=>r.Mailbox==Model.Mailbox)){
<article class="import-message"><h3>Gmail message @mail.MessageId</h3>
<a class="text-link" href="@("https://mail.google.com/mail/?authuser="+Uri.EscapeDataString(mail.Mailbox)+"#all/"+Uri.EscapeDataString(mail.MessageId))" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read original email in Gmail</a>
<form method="post" asp-page-handler="RecheckComplaint"><input type="hidden" name="MessageId" value="@mail.MessageId"/>
<label class="check-row consent"><input type="checkbox" name="Permission" value="true" required/><span>I checked this email. Treat it as a complaint and retain/process it using the configured AI service.</span></label>
<button type="submit" class="button primary">Recheck as complaint</button></form>
<form method="post" asp-page-handler="DismissNonComplaint"><input type="hidden" name="MessageId" value="@mail.MessageId"/><button type="submit" class="button secondary">Dismiss review reference</button></form>
</article>}
<p class="field-help">Queued requests run before normal collection, up to 20 per run. Fetch/OCR failures retry; unsupported messages move to manual review. Paused automation stays paused.</p></section>}
<section class="panel form-panel"><span class="eyebrow">ONE REVIEW STEP</span><h2>@Model.Queue.Count prepared complaints</h2><p class="muted">Extracted source text and Gmail references remain intact. Missing facts and uncertain routes are flagged rather than invented.</p>
@if(Model.Queue.Count==0){<p>No prepared complaints yet. Enable intake or run the social demo below.</p>}
@foreach(var row in Model.Queue){var p=row.Proposal;var a=p.Analysis;var missing=a.District.Length<2||a.Location.Length<2||a.Route.Department=="review";<article class="import-message"><div class="panel-heading"><h3>@p.Draft.Title</h3><span class="badge draft">@(missing?"Needs details":"Ready for review")</span></div><p>@p.Source @(p.IsDemo?"· Fictional demo":"")</p><p>@CaseRules.Departments[a.Route.Department] · @PilotRoutingCatalog.CategoryLabel(a.Route.Category) · @PilotRoutingCatalog.IssueLabel(a.Route.Subcategory)</p><p>District: @(a.District.Length>0?a.District:"Missing") · Location: @(a.Location.Length>0?a.Location:"Missing")</p><p class="field-help">@p.Draft.Method</p><a class="button primary" href="/Automation/Review/@p.InboxId">Review prepared complaint</a></article>}
</section>
<section class="panel form-panel"><span class="eyebrow">SOCIAL MONITORING PROTOTYPE</span><h2>X, Facebook and Instagram</h2><p><strong>Facebook and Instagram live collection remain pending.</strong> <a href="/XSettings">Configure live X public search</a> for bounded, on-demand collection into Intake inbox. X imports use local review and are excluded from this automatic AI preparation queue. This demo delivers three fictional posts through the collection, extraction and draft-preparation queue. It never logs in to or crawls a social platform.</p><form method="post" asp-page-handler="Demo" data-busy><label class="check-row consent"><input asp-for="Permission" required/><span>Process the three fictional social posts using the configured AI service when available.</span></label><button class="button secondary">Run social feed demo</button></form><p class="field-help">Repeated runs reuse source IDs. Demo cases are marked Sample after approval and excluded from normal analytics by default.</p></section>
